# Design-authority bundles are byte-preserved.
#
# These files ARE the executable specification (Pattern 30 / the Design
# Authority discipline). Their integrity is asserted by SHA-256 in
# docs/design-authority/**/SHA256SUMS and by a checksum test. Letting git
# renormalize line endings on checkout silently changes those bytes and
# fails the integrity check on a file nobody edited — which is exactly the
# false alarm that erodes trust in a governance control.
#
# -text disables all EOL conversion for the tracked bundle sources.
docs/design-authority/** -text
